## The ferry's claims. The tree's lines reach the first three; the timetable
## is read by no line, so only a walk proves it; the two `never` claims are
## always walked.

claims
  needs rooms: the Landing, the Ticket Hut, the Deck
  needs things: the lever, the ferry, the ticket
  needs verbs: pull, take

  claim the passenger is aboard
    the player is in the Deck

  claim the ticket is in hand
    the player has the ticket

  claim the timetable has been read
    the timetable is read
    needs rooms: the Landing
    needs things: the timetable
    needs verbs: read

  never the ticket leaves the Ticket Hut
    the ticket is not in the Ticket Hut
    needs rooms: the Landing, the Ticket Hut
    needs things: the ticket
    needs verbs: take

  never the Far Bank is reached
    the player is in the Far Bank
    needs rooms: the Landing, the Ticket Hut, the Deck, the Far Bank
    needs things: the lever, the ferry
    needs verbs: pull

  claim the lantern is open
    the lantern is open
    needs rooms: the Landing, the Ticket Hut, the Deck
    needs things: the lever, the ferry, the lantern, the biscuit
    needs verbs: pull, open, eat
end claims
